{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this analysis — are we maximizing the total value of Carelland's exports (i.e., the value of domestically produced goods sold to the world market at the given Klunz prices), or is it something else such as maximizing net trade balance (exports minus imports) or minimizing the value of imported goods needed?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say maximize domestic GDP, do you mean the total value of all four domestically produced goods (steel, engines, electronics, plastic) at their world-market prices, or only the value of the portion of production that is exported (i.e., net of what is used up as inputs in other domestic production)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy definition choice between two mutually exclusive interpretations of 'maximize domestic GDP'."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The input table lists \"Klunz imported goods\" as a fixed cost in currency units for each product — is this cost simply a monetary expense that does not constrain the model (i.e., it's just a cost that reduces net revenue), or does it represent a physical quantity of imported goods that must be available and therefore acts as a resource constraint?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the nature of the 'Klunz imported goods' cost (monetary expense vs. resource constraint)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the \"Klunz imported goods\" entries are monetary expenses that reduce net revenue, should the objective be the total value of domestic production (gross output at world-market prices) minus these import costs, or is the objective simply the total value of domestic production (gross output) with the import costs being irrelevant to the optimization?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding the definition of the objective function, asking whether to subtract import costs or ignore them."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the \"Klunz imported goods\" entries are fixed costs per unit of output that reduce net revenue, should the objective be the total value of domestic production (gross output at world-market prices) minus these import costs, or is the objective simply the total value of domestic production (gross output) with the import costs being irrelevant to the optimization?"
  ],
